@title Overdue fines: three proposals compared
@subtitle For Thursday's library board meeting. Baseline is last year's circulation report; proposals A, B and C are weighed against it.
@width wide

! Read this first. This page is static: it cannot take typed assumptions or move sliders. Every figure marked "derived" is arithmetic on the circulation report. Where a proposal's effect depends on something the report does not contain, the page says so and lists the assumption you would have to supply (see "Assumptions to settle").

## Where things stand today

kpi Fines billed | $84,650.20 | 12 branches, last year
kpi Fines collected | $32,002.55 | 37.8% of billed | bad
kpi Not collected | $52,647.65 | billed minus collected
kpi Cardholders blocked | 3,876 | 12 branches

Totals are derived by adding the branch rows. They include Lakeside (seasonal) and Veterans' Branch, North, whose billed figure has lost-item fees mixed in.

The most important number for a board deciding on revenue: if every fine disappeared, the most revenue that could be lost is what is collected today, $32,002.55, not the $84,650.20 billed.

